  "name": "Example: Expressing a Set Using a Conditional Definition",
  "problem": "Describe the set $S = \\{-9,-8,-7, ..., 5\\}$ using a conditional definition.",
  "worked_solution": "The set $S$ contains all integer numbers between $-9$ and $5$ (including $-9$ and $5$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS = \\{ x \\in \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\mathbb Z} \\: : \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-9} \\leq x \\leq \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}5} \\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example, we can write $S$ equivalently as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{ x \\in \\mathbb Z \\: : \\: -10 \\lt x \\lt 6 \\big\\}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
